      "side": 1,
      "message": "@zhidou@google.com,\nHi, I saw you are working on library to read the trunk stable flag.\nAs this is a first use case in our team to read flag value from module and platform, could you help to confirm my understanding? \n\nIn this CL,`refactor_socket_destroy_on_removed_address` is defined under \"com.android.tethering\" container and both module code and platform code check this flag.\n\nThe flag value module and platform code see will be the flag value at module build time.\nSo, when the device install module built with flag disabled, platform code see flag is disabled.\nAnd if the device install newer module built with flag enabled, platform code see flag is enabled.\nAlso, the flag value does not change while device is running since the module update requires reboot.\n\nIs my understanding correct?\nAlso, do you see any issue in FlaggedApi.bp and flags.aconfig to share the flag between modules and platform?",
      "revId": "33966aed37cc39cc1815bcb8badf46a6b0497a1c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
